What these labels are, and are not
----------------------------------

Two properties of this dataset are licence-independent but matter for any use,
and are stated here because a licence file is the one document people do read:

1. The 5,222 behaviour labels are TEACHER labels produced by a 5-pass
   Qwen3-VL-235B ensemble, not by a human. The full vote distribution is
   included rather than only the majority, because the margin predicts human
   agreement. Treat them as a strong automatic annotation, not ground truth.

2. The 456 human labels measure AGREEMENT, not accuracy: every one was collected
   with the model's suggestion visible on screen, and each record carries an
   `assisted` flag set to true.

The footage itself is not distributed under this licence and is not included in
this repository. It is observational recording of a single animal held at a
partner aquarium; `README.md` describes how to reconstruct the clips from the
provenance recorded in the labels.

